{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Celebrating Christmas", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Flashback", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 18, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn6le18ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Present Perfect Tense versus The Simple Past Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about a finished action or event that is connected to the present in some way.</p> You use the Simple Past tense to talk about a finished action or event <span class=\"strong\">not</span> connected to the present.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Look at the chart about how to form the Present Perfect tense:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We use <span class=\"strong\">have/has</span> + <span class=\"strong\">the past participle</span> of the verb in Present Perfect sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past tense form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past participle form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"see\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"saw\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"seen\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I've never seen ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"get\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"got\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"gotten/got\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I haven't got ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"skate\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"skated\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"skated\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I haven't skated ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"finish\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"finished\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"finished\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When we've finished ...\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I haven't skated for a long time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I haven't got any skates.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When we've finished we can come back here.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Did someone build a rink in their backyard? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It wasn't as crowded.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Used to and Would to Talk About Past Habits", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Used to</span> and <span class=\"strong\">would</span> are both used to talk about actions that happened in the past. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "We use <span class=\"italic\">used to</span> to express a past  action or state that is no longer happening. It uses -ed to show past tense.</p>  For example: She used to ride her bike every day.</br>  (Before, she rode her bike every day, but now she doesn't ride everyday.)</p>  My cousins used to play in the snow all day long. </br> (Before, they played in the snow all day long, but now they don't play in the snow.)</p>  We can use <span class=\"italic\">would </span>  to express repeated past actions and past routines.</p>  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I used to go to the swimming pool every day. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I don't do this anymore.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She would get a large coffee after lunch.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It was her habit in the past.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I used to play hockey with the other kids a lot. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We would play on the street if it wasn't cold enough to make ice.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They used to make ice?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We would play until we were too cold to continue.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "backyard", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an area behind a house ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sometimes we had a rink in our backyard. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le18ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about Christmas activities.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "hockey", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a game played on ice with sticks and a puck ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We would play hockey all day long. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le18ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to skate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to use skates to move on ice", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We skated at the Boston Common. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le18ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to build", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to construct; to make ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We built a skating rink in our backyard.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le18ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "clever", "type": "name"}, {"content": "intelligent ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Skating was a clever way to keep the kids active at Christmas. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le18ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to reheat ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to heat again after it is cold.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We can reheat the leftovers for dinner.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le18ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Make a list of 6 activities you used to do as a child.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write sentences saying where you would do these activities.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Include who you used to go with and when you used to do the activities.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your sentences to a partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I make a list of activities I did as a child.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write sentences for each activity.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I say where and when I used to do the activities.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I say who used to go with.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my sentences aloud.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn6le18ob09re2img01.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn6le18ob09re2img01.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I used to skate sometimes when I was young, but never on Christmas Day.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I used to play hockey with the other kids a lot. We would play on the street if it wasn't cold enough to make ice.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: They used to make ice?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Did someone build a rink in their backyard? </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Yeah. We would play until we were too cold to continue. Mom would make a vat of fries for us!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I've never seen a backyard ice rink."}, {"image": "engenn6le18ob09re2img02.jpg", "time": "23000", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Some people worked on one for weeks. It would keep all of us kids outside for hours.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Sounds like it was a clever way to keep you busy!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I haven't skated for a long time. Why not go next week on New Year's Day?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I haven't got any skates.  </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: We can rent them."}, {"image": "engenn6le18ob09re2img03.jpg", "time": "37500", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I'll whip up some hot chocolate and treats.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: We used to go to the rink early. It wasn't as crowded.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: When we've finished we can come back here after and reheat leftovers.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: It's a date!"}], "audiosrc": "engenn6le18ob09re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn6le18ob09re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [], "audiosrc": "engenn6le18ob09re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn6le18ob09re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "picture"}], "id": 2}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data":